  "question": {
    "text": "From the top of a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>64</mn></math> metres high tower, a stone is thrown upwards vertically with the velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>48</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The greatest height (in metres) attained by the stone, assuming the value of the gravitational acceleration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, is:"
  },
